course: dictionary
lesson: 16145
title: Willingness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Willingness is a noun, a name for a quality a person has. It means being happy or ready to do something when someone asks. A person with willingness does not need to be asked twice.
explain: Read the clues in the sentence: «She shows great willingness to help.» The word «help» tells you what she is ready to do, and «great» tells you how ready she is. So willingness must mean she is glad and keen to help.
explain: Use the swap check. Put in a word that fits the meaning: «She shows great readiness to help» still makes sense, so readiness is close to willingness. If your swapped word makes the sentence silly, your meaning is wrong.
fact: Willingness is a noun, so it names a quality a person has.
fact: Willingness means being happy or ready to do something when asked.
fact: Willingness is closely linked to the word willing, which means ready and happy to do something.
fact: In school reports, teachers may write: «She shows great willingness to learn.»
fact: Willingness is uncountable, so we say «great willingness», not «a willingness».
exercise: «She shows great willingness to help.» What does willingness mean? | *Being happy and ready to help when asked | Forgetting something important | Shouting loudly in class | Being too tired to move
exercise: «The team showed willingness to learn new games.» Which word has the same meaning as willingness here? | Boredom | Silence | *Readiness | Refusal
exercise: Which sentence shows willingness? | The dog refused to walk | Mia hid under the desk and said nothing | *Ben put his hand up at once and said, «I will tidy the room.» | The class groaned when the teacher asked for help
test: Ali says, «I can help carry the chairs!» What does his willingness show? | Ali is angry with the teacher | Ali is tired and wants to go home | Ali is lost | *Ali is happy and ready to help
test: Which word best fits? «The new pupil showed great ___ to join the club.» | Silence | *Willingness | Hurry | Sadness
exam: In the sentence «Her willingness to learn impressed the teacher», what is the best meaning of willingness? | Being too tired to learn | *Being happy and ready to learn when asked | Being sad about school | Not wanting to learn anything
